{"id":"08babcd57560d642","group":"58","path":"58/batch04/58-thm-post-problem.md","title":"Post's Problem","display":"thm-post-problem — Post's Problem","type":"theorem","metadata":{"type":"theorem","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-thm-post-problem","aliases":["58-thm-post-problem"],"display":"thm-post-problem — Post's Problem","depends_on":["[[../batch03/58-df-turing-degree.md]]","[[../batch06/58-df-turing-reducible.md]]","[[../batch20/58-df-zfc-recursion3-recursively-enumerable-set.md]]","[[../batch03/58-df-zfc-recursion2-oracle-computation.md]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"theorem"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-thm-post-problem"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-thm-post-problem</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"thm-post-problem — Post's Problem"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"227c7eaf354f0ec0\" href=\"?note=227c7eaf354f0ec0\" title=\"../batch03/58-df-turing-degree.md\">../batch03/58-df-turing-degree.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"7f65c348d236e554\" href=\"?note=7f65c348d236e554\" title=\"../batch06/58-df-turing-reducible.md\">../batch06/58-df-turing-reducible.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"618dc6ad8d6c1e22\" href=\"?note=618dc6ad8d6c1e22\" title=\"../batch20/58-df-zfc-recursion3-recursively-enumerable-set.md\">../batch20/58-df-zfc-recursion3-recursively-enumerable-set.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-4\" data-note=\"1d725a0797bae6df\" href=\"?note=1d725a0797bae6df\" title=\"../batch03/58-df-zfc-recursion2-oracle-computation.md\">../batch03/58-df-zfc-recursion2-oracle-computation.md</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"A,K\\subseteq\\omega\">\\(A,K\\subseteq\\omega\\)</span></li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\leq_T\">\\(\\leq_T\\)</span> (Turing reducibility from dependency)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"K\\coloneqq\\{e\\in\\omega:\\exists y\\in\\omega\\;\\mathrm{ZfcRecursion2OracleComputation}_S(y,e,\\varnothing,e)\\}\">\\(K\\coloneqq\\{e\\in\\omega:\\exists y\\in\\omega\\;\\mathrm{ZfcRecursion2OracleComputation}_S(y,e,\\varnothing,e)\\}\\)</span>，采用 <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-5\" data-note=\"227c7eaf354f0ec0\" href=\"?note=227c7eaf354f0ec0\" title=\"58-df-turing-degree.md\">58-df-turing-degree.md</a> 的同一停机集合。</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{ZfcRecursion3RecursivelyEnumerableSet}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{ZfcRecursion3RecursivelyEnumerableSet}_S\\)</span> (c.e.-set predicate from dependency)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}post\\text{-}problem}\\vdash\n\\exists A\\subseteq\\omega\\;\n\\left[\n\\mathrm{ZfcRecursion3RecursivelyEnumerableSet}_S(A)\n\\land\\varnothing\\leq_T A\n\\land\\neg(A\\leq_T\\varnothing)\n\\land A\\leq_T K\n\\land\\neg(K\\leq_T A)\n\\right].\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}post\\text{-}problem}\\vdash\n\\exists A\\subseteq\\omega\\;\n\\left[\n\\mathrm{ZfcRecursion3RecursivelyEnumerableSet}_S(A)\n\\land\\varnothing\\leq_T A\n\\land\\neg(A\\leq_T\\varnothing)\n\\land A\\leq_T K\n\\land\\neg(K\\leq_T A)\n\\right].\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Post (1944) 猜想存在非递归的递归可枚举集</li>\n<li>断言表达存在非递归且不完备的递归可枚举 Turing 度。</li>\n<li>Friedberg-Muchnik (1956) 肯定了这个问题</li>\n<li>构造了两互不包含的 r.e. 度</li>\n<li>打破了递归可枚举集的分类</li>\n<li>应用：证明 r.e. 度结构是复杂的</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remar